body:
Found by the sibling-tab sweep ordered on objectui#5110 (References panel). This is a **measurement**, filed unassigned for PM triage — not fixed in PR for #5110.

## The reading

`packages/app-shell/src/views/metadata-admin/AuditPanel.tsx`, the `load` callback (locate by text, not line number):

```ts
try {
  const res = await client.audit(type, name, { limit: 100 });
  setEvents(res.events ?? []);
} catch (err: any) {
  setError(String(err?.message ?? err));
  setEvents([]);
} finally {
  setLoading(false);
}
```

The catch sets an error **and** zeroes `events`. The render then shows all three of these at once:

- the failure, in a rose banner — `{error && ...}`
- the header count, `{events?.length ?? 0} {t('engine.edit.auditCount', locale)}` → **`0 events`**
- the empty state, because the very next branch is `!events || events.length === 0`:
  `engine.edit.auditEmptyTitle` = "No audit events yet",
  `engine.edit.auditEmptyDescription` = "No save, publish, rollback, delete or reset attempts have been recorded for this item. Once someone tries to change it (allowed or denied), the attempt will appear here."

## Why this is weaker than #5110, and why it is still a finding

Unlike the References panel, the failure **is** visible here — the banner renders — so nothing is silently swallowed and this is not the same severity. What is wrong is that a positive claim about the record ("no save, publish, rollback, delete or reset attempts have been recorded for this item") and a measured count of `0` are rendered *simultaneously with* the statement that the measurement failed. The two contradict each other, and the operator has to know which one to believe. An audit tab is read for compliance-shaped questions ("did anyone touch this?"), so the false zero is the part that matters.

The minimal shape is the one #5110 landed: make the failure its own arm so the empty state and the count are reachable only from a completed read. `HistoryPanel`, `RelatedPanel` and `DiagnosticsPage` on the same page already do this (see the control query below) — this panel is the odd one out.

Severity is deliberately not asserted here; #5110's own card records that severity judged at filing time is unreliable in both directions. Filed plainly for the PM's triage round.

## Sweep control query — the zero elsewhere is a measurement, not a broken search

The #5110 sweep covered every same-page loader that can fail. Three of them already hold the three-state shape, which is what proves the sweep could see the pattern it was looking for:

- **history** — `ResourceHistoryPage.tsx`: `catch` sets `error` only; `events` is left alone. Clean.
- **related** — `RelatedPanel.tsx`: per-group `error` field; renders `!g.loading && g.error` before `!g.loading && !g.error && matches.length === 0`. Clean.
- **diagnostics** — `DiagnosticsPage.tsx`: `{!loading && error && ...loadFailed}` and `{!loading && !error && groups.length === 0 && ...clean}` — mutually exclusive by construction. Clean.
- **audit** — this card.

## Dedup

Searched open issues for the audit panel's empty state, for `catch`-swallowed failures rendered as empty results, and for AuditPanel by name; nothing covering this. Control: the same search family returns objectui#4408 ("A list request that 404s with `OBJECT_API_DISABLED` renders as the generic empty state", closed) and #5110 itself, so the zero is a measurement rather than a dead query. No duplicate.

## Related

objectui#5110 (the References panel, same class, fixed) · objectstack#9426 (the producer-side defect on the audit route) · ADR-0110 D3, "a miss and a fault are different facts"
